<div class="preamble-box">
  <strong>Central Theme:</strong> Based primarily on <em>LM</em> I:36 (<span class="kt">"Bikarav Alai M'ray'im"</span>) and I:60 (<span class="kt">"Pasach Rabbi Shimon"</span>). The essential trial of every person is <span class="kt">ta'avas na'uf</span> — the lust of immorality — which is the collective root of all the evil desires and evil character traits of the seventy nations. Against it stand the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov, the seventy luminous faces of Torah. Wine stands precisely at this balance-point — the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — aspiring to include all seventy faces of Torah, yet vulnerable to drawing all seventy nations' evil. The laws of <span class="kt">yayin nesech</span> illuminate the cosmic stakes of this battle, the role of the <span class="kt">tzaddikim</span>, the printing press, free choice, martyrdom, strife, and the coming of Mashiach.
  <span class="source-ref">Drawing also on <em>LM</em> I:19, I:23, II:7, II:26, II:68 and many further teachings.</span>
